docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-10.md:772:| 36 | (no sentence; A9 states no rule for verifier releases made before release-key independence is established) | A9:326-332 | "Every verifier release made before the first public verifier release is signed with a separate TEST release key; its public key is never published as the release key, never named in the freeze record or relying-party text, and never introduced by a production release. A pre-gate TEST signature cannot authenticate a production release. Production authentication must use the independently authenticated production release key and must reject TEST authority, including TEST provisioning overrides. This does not protect a user who skips authentication or acquires a substituted initial key. No pre-gate artifact is offered for production reliance. Before the first public verifier release, a rehearsal must show that an otherwise correct archive with only a TEST signature is refused by the production acquisition and verification procedure, including when the TEST key is supplied through the test interface." (A10.4.2) **AUTHOR ADOPTED 2026-10-18** (recommended by the owner and Codex) | GATE | G |
